{
    "background_story": "Tootsie was a majestic mare born on the vast, rolling steppe of Mongolia. She roamed the open grasslands with her herd, her mane and tail flowing in the wind. As a foal, Tootsie was drawn to the nomadic herders who traversed the steppe, and she would often follow them, fascinated by their way of life. As she grew, Tootsie became a prized companion to a young herder named Temujin, who rode her across the steppe, herding sheep and goats. Together, they explored the endless expanse of the steppe, facing fierce storms and blistering sun. Tootsie's strength, agility, and endurance made her an invaluable partner, and she earned the respect and admiration of Temujin and the entire tribe. She became a symbol of the steppe's wild beauty and the unbreakable bond between humans and animals.",
